PHASE 2 - CATALOGUE AND OVERLAP ANALYSIS (documents only)

1. Assign every existing validator a catalogue entry:
     id         FAMILY-NN (e.g. ERR-02). Keep a mapping column to the old
                name AND to the identifier the REST receiver knows. The REST
                identifier never changes.
     family     STR structure | CFW compiler-framework | ERR exceptions |
                CTL control flow | ACC access reuse / repeated object access |
                PRF other performance | DAT data/types/literals | MEM memory |
                TXN transactions/side effects | LYR layering/imports |
                NAM naming | MNT maintainability | FMT formatting
     level      Token | Stmt | Block | Method | Package | Cross
     concern    the ONE question it answers, in 2-4 words
     anchor     what it inspects: a node type (for_stmt, handler...), a shared
                fact (access paths, loops), or raw text
     input_kind regex-text | line | ast | mixed
     severity, profile (kernel / house)
2. Overlap analysis, both ways:
   a) Static: list validators that share family+concern, share an anchor and
      look for the same construct, call each other, or duplicate helper
      logic (e.g. two different ways of finding "the same object accessed
      twice in a block").
   b) Empirical: from baseline/legacy.csv build a co-firing matrix - for each
      pair of rules, how many times they fire on the same source and
      overlapping line range. Include 5 sample rows per non-zero pair.
3. Classify each overlap:
     DUPLICATE    same concern -> merge into one rule
     NESTED       one is a special case of the other -> exclusive_with +
                  precedence (the more specific wins)
     SHARED-FACT  same underlying analysis done twice -> compute once in a
                  shared facts layer, both rules read it
     COINCIDENT   different concerns that happen to hit the same line -> fine,
                  allow-list it
4. Write docs/refactor/CATALOG.md (table of all entries) and
   docs/refactor/OVERLAPS.md (matrix, classification, proposed fix per pair,
   and which baseline rows each fix would change).
STOP. Report the catalogue size per family and the overlap list. Wait for me
to approve the classification.

