PHASE 3 - RESTRUCTURE WITHOUT BEHAVIOUR CHANGE

Target layout (adapt names to the repo; protected files stay where they are):

  <app_package>/
    audit_core/            # FROZEN after this phase; changes are separate tasks
      model.py             # Node (type, line, end_line, start, end, attrs,
                           #  children, parent) and Finding dataclasses
      adapter.py           # existing Lark tree -> Node. The ONLY module that
                           #  knows Lark. Reuse the existing grammar/parser.
      source.py            # comment masking (positions kept), --@NoCheck(...)
                           #  suppression, '-- expect: ID' markers for fixtures
      facts.py             # computed once per source: access paths (root,
                           #  segments, enclosing method/loops, read/write,
                           #  call-statement), loops and their variant names
      rule.py              # RuleSpec (id, version, family, title, level,
                           #  concern, severity, profiles, node_types,
                           #  precedence, exclusive_with, legacy_name,
                           #  rest_id) + Rule base (visit(node, ctx) or
                           #  check(ctx)) + finding() helper
      registry.py          # EXPLICIT list: from .rules import err_02, ...
                           #  RULES = [err_02.Rule(), ...]; validate():
                           #  unique ids, unique (family, concern),
                           #  exclusive_with symmetric with distinct precedence
      engine.py            # prepare -> parse -> facts -> ONE tree walk that
                           #  dispatches each node to rules subscribed to its
                           #  type -> facts-based checks -> profile filter ->
                           #  suppressions -> resolve (exclusive rules on
                           #  related subjects: lower precedence wins) -> sort
      legacy_bridge.py     # Finding -> the EXACT existing result object the
                           #  JSON builder already consumes. Payload builder
                           #  and REST client stay untouched.
    rules/
      __init__.py          # explicit imports only
      err_02.py, acc_01.py, ...   # one Rule class per file, file name = id
  tests/
    fixtures/<RULE-ID>/pos_*.avq | neg_*.avq | edge_*.avq
    test_catalog.py        # registry validates; every rule has >=1 pos and
                           #  >=1 neg; no orphan fixture folders; semver
    test_fixtures.py       # EVERY fixture runs through ALL rules; actual
                           #  {(rule_id, line)} must equal its '-- expect:'
                           #  markers exactly (catches overlap automatically)
    test_payload_contract.py
  tools/  run_corpus.py, baseline_diff.py, snapshot_payload.py,
          scope_guard.py (fails if files outside the named rule changed),
          check.py (cross-platform: pytest -> scope_guard -> corpus ->
          baseline diff; prints a one-screen summary)
  docs/refactor/ INVENTORY.md, CATALOG.md, OVERLAPS.md, PROGRESS.md,
                 PROPOSALS.md
  CLAUDE.md               # the working rules below, for future sessions

Order of work:
  1. Build audit_core with the bridge, and wire ONE call site: where the app
     currently loops over validators, call the engine instead. Keep the old
     loop available behind a single switch until all validators are moved.
     Change nothing in P1–P5.
  2. Move validators one at a time into rules/<id>.py. Keep their logic;
     only change how they receive input (Node/facts instead of re-parsing
     or re-scanning) where that is mechanical and provably equivalent.
     Text/regex validators may keep regex for now but must run on the
     comment-masked text from source.py.
  3. For each moved validator, harvest fixtures: take 3-5 real lines from
     baseline/legacy.csv where it fires (pos_) and 3-5 where a similar
     construct does NOT fire (neg_), trimmed into minimal parseable sources.
  4. After EACH validator: run tools/check.py <ID>. Gate: tests green,
     scope OK, baseline diff EMPTY (zero +/-), payload snapshots equal.
     Commit. Update PROGRESS.md.
  5. When all are moved, remove the old loop and the switch. Full check:
     diff still empty.
  6. Rebuild the executable with the EXISTING build command, unchanged, and
     run the built exe in offline/dry mode on 5 corpus files if the app
     supports it. If it doesn't, report how I should smoke-test it.
STOP after every 5 validators with a progress report.

